  "prompt": "You are the coding agent of the imports team. You can use the tools provided.\n\nIssue #412: invoice imports crash on dates such as \"2026/03/05\" and \"05.03.2026\" (day first). Fix the issue. Then write pr.json with \"summary\" (one sentence), \"ci_status\" (\"green\" or \"red\", from your last test run) and \"failing_tests\" (a list, empty if none). When you are done, reply with a short summary.",
  "final_response": "I have fixed the issue where invoice imports were crashing on dates with forward slashes (\"YYYY/MM/DD\") or dots (\"DD.MM.YYYY\"). I updated the `parse_date` function in `app/parser.py` to recognize these separators and parse the dates accordingly, while maintaining support for the standard ISO format (\"YYYY-MM-DD\") via the existing `split_date` helper. All tests, including those for the new formats, are now passing.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Updated the date parser to support YYYY/MM/DD and DD.MM.YYYY formats, resolving crashes during invoice imports.\",\n  \"ci_status\": \"green\",\n  \"failing_tests\": []\n}\n```",
